You are drafting Zephyr-ready test steps for a manual test case.
The objective below is finalized (user-reviewed). Derive the steps from it.

An objective bullet states an END STATE — what should be true. A step is a PROCEDURE — what
a tester does to show it. Re-wording a bullet is not a step, whatever verb it opens with.
"Verify …" is a perfectly good way to begin a real step; the fault is restatement, never the
word.

Keep the steps as high-level as the case allows: say what to do, and what to confirm, in
plain words, and leave the detail to the tester.

## Case
{{ case_key }}{% if primary and primary.w %} — {{ primary.w }}{% endif %}

## Finalized objective (authoritative)
{{ objective }}
{% if testlink_selections %}
## TestLink selections (evidence of what has been tested before)
{% for s in testlink_selections %}- {{ s.id_or_key }}: {{ s.title }}
{% endfor %}{% endif %}{% if zephyr_selections %}
## Zephyr exemplars (evidence)
{% for s in zephyr_selections %}- {{ s.key or s.id_or_key }}: {{ s.title }}
{% endfor %}{% endif %}{% if atp_selections %}
## ATPyLib coverage (selected ART)
